Cipher.

purpose: def"
Universal CE-OS source-to-QPS syntax and topology converter.

Cipher learns the syntax and dependency topology of a supported source language
and writes the QPS syntax and repository topology that express the same program.
It does not invent a source-neutral object model, reinterpret source identities,
or make runtime representations into authored QPS concepts.
";

mission: (
input- "Supported source-language syntax, names, module boundaries, imports, and directory topology";
translation- "Map each supported source syntax form to its proven QPS syntax equivalent without changing authored identities";
topology- "Preserve the local source dependency tree as the equivalent QPS directory and module tree";
foreign- "Separate external dependencies from local dependencies and materialize required external dependency topology beneath the translated module's local libs directory";
proof- "Only exact translated candidate bytes that pass support inspection and QPS validation may be published";
);

pipeline: (
prepare- "parse source syntax into CipherDocument and CipherNode translation IR while preserving source names and relationships";
closure- "recursively discover local source dependencies and classify unresolved external dependencies before publication";
project- "project each local source file to the corresponding QPS path without flattening directory topology";
translate- "source syntax -> proven QPS syntax equivalents";
support- "reject any source syntax whose exact QPS equivalent has not been proven";
emit- "emit the translated QPS candidate directly from the supported source syntax";
validate- "validate the exact emitted candidate with QPS";
plan- "ConversionPlan freezes source, destination, dependency truth, support truth, topology, and exact candidate bytes";
publish- "publish only the exact candidate bytes already validated by the plan";
);

ownership: (
canonical_root- "qps/cipher";
authored_orchestration- "qps/qps/cipher.qps owns QPS-authored command orchestration";
engineering_role- "Engineering is a Cipher consumer and may provide domain-specific source information, but does not own universal Cipher translation";
library_boundary- "External dependencies belong beneath the local libs directory of the translated module context rather than a repository-global Cipher namespace";
);

source_model: (
universal- "Each source language is understood through its own syntax adapter";
supported_current- "Python, C++, JSON, YAML";
ir- "CipherDocument and CipherNode preserve source syntax facts needed to select exact QPS equivalents; they are implementation machinery, not a replacement authored data model";
identity- "Variable, function, class, module, field, and alias names survive translation unchanged unless QPS syntax requires exact escaping";
);

structural_model: (
repository_namespace- "QPS itself is the destination library and structural namespace: filesystem/file -> key -> term -> nested term -> item/value";
reference- "[>folder/file.key.term.item-] resolves existing authored QPS structure";
inline- "[< code] is the canonical QPS Inline source-input surface";
package_index- "A source package __init__.py projects to the corresponding QPS _index.qps";
mapping_rule- "A Python mapping remains mapping_expression translation IR until its exact native QPS syntax equivalent is proven; RuntimeValue RECORD and record(...) do not authorize generic mapping translation";
json_yaml_rule- "JSON and YAML mappings already translate through native QPS Term and Item structure rather than anonymous record(...) values";
sequence_rule- "Python list syntax may translate to canonical QPS sequence(...) because that authored syntax is proven; the runtime value does not itself establish the authority";
runtime_boundary- "Runtime representations implement machine behavior and never create a second authored QPS identity system";
);

topology_contract: (
entry- "Translation begins at the requested source entry such as run.py";
local_closure- "Every recursively resolved local dependency is translated as its own corresponding QPS file";
preserve_paths- "Relative local directory and module topology survives conversion";
preserve_calls- "Call relationships and source symbol relationships survive conversion";
preserve_import_identity- "Local import relationships become references to the corresponding translated local QPS identities without flattening the source tree";
no_consolidation- "Cipher does not consolidate a local dependency tree into one artifact merely because dependency resolution can see the whole closure";
foreign_locality- "External dependencies are materialized beneath libs in the same translated directory or module context that owns the dependency boundary";
foreign_topology- "External package and module topology is preserved beneath that local libs directory";
);

conversion_contract: (
question- "For each source construct ask: what is the QPS syntax and topology equivalent of this source syntax and topology?";
no_renaming- "Do not rename source variables, functions, classes, modules, fields, or aliases as a translation strategy";
no_remodeling- "Do not replace source data relationships with a Cipher-designed dictionary, record, object, or source-neutral authored model";
no_runtime_inference- "Do not choose authored QPS syntax merely because a runtime type resembles a source-language value";
no_approximation- "Unsupported source syntax remains a blocker rather than being silently omitted, approximated, or redesigned";
no_retranslation_publish- "Publication writes the exact candidate bytes frozen and validated by the ready ConversionPlan";
no_overwrite- "Cipher does not silently replace an existing destination";
atomicity- "Multi-file publication preserves all-or-nothing behavior";
);

python_contract: (
entry_rule- "Starting from a Python entry file, recursively follow every local import required by that program";
local_rule- "Local Python modules translate to corresponding QPS modules at equivalent relative paths";
package_rule- "__init__.py translates to _index.qps";
external_rule- "Python dependencies that are not local workspace modules are external and belong beneath the translated module context's libs directory";
syntax_rule- "Python constructs are translated only when their exact QPS syntax equivalent is established";
named_arguments- "Python keyword call arguments preserve their original names through QPS named call syntax";
lists- "Python list expressions translate to proven QPS sequence(...) syntax";
dicts- "Python dict expressions remain blocked as mapping_expression until their exact native QPS syntax equivalent is established";
);

rules: (
qps_authority- "QPS authored syntax and topology are the destination authority; Cipher may not invent QPS language surfaces";
implementation_boundary- "Parser IR, runtime values, and host containers are implementation machinery rather than authored structural identities";
tests- "Regression tests must prove identity preservation, syntax equivalence, topology preservation, support truth, exact-candidate validation, and atomic publication";
current_task- "qps/qps/checklist.qps task cipher.foreign_and_structured_semantics remains active until the real Engineering witness has complete direct QPS syntax coverage";
);


completion: (
authority- "The agent assigned cipher.foreign_and_structured_semantics owns routine completion judgment against qps/qps/checklist.qps";
index_rule- "Finished Cipher semantics must be reflected in this _index.qps before checklist acceptance";
save_rule- "Once authored finish conditions and regressions are proven, transition the task to complete and run qps save without an additional operator confirmation";
git_rule- "After successful save and final verification, stage only Cipher task-owned files and create the task checkpoint commit while preserving unrelated dirty work";
);
